1000000100001011":1,"111111011111000001100000000000111110001111110111111111":2,"111111011111000001100100000011011111110111001000000000":2,"111111011111000001100100000011011111110111111011110100":1,"111111011111000001100100000011100001111000111111111111":1,"111111011111000001100100000011111111111111111111111111":4,"111111011111001111100011110000000000000000000000000000":1,"111111011111001111100011110000000000000000110011110100":1,"111111011111001111100011110000011110000111110011110100":2,"111111011111001111100011110000100000001000000100001011":2,"111111011111001111100011110000100000001000110111111111":1,"111111011111001111100011110000111110001111000100001011":1,"111111011111001111100011110000111110001111110111111111":2,"111111011111001111100111110011000001110000001000000000":1,"111111011111001111100111110011011111110111111011110100":3,"111111011111001111100111110011100001111000001100001011":2,"111111011111001111100111110011111111111111001100001011":2,"111111011111001111100111110011111111111111111111111111":1,"111111111111110001111000001100000000000000000000000000":1,"111111111111110001111000001100100000001000110111111111":1,"111111111111110001111000001100111110001111110111111111":2,"111111111111110001111100001111000001110000111011110100":1,"111111111111110001111100001111011111110111001000000000":1,"111111111111110001111100001111011111110111111011110100":1,"111111111111110001111100001111100001111000001100001011":1,"111111111111110001111100001111100001111000111111111111":2,"111111111111110001111100001111111111111111001100001011":2,"111111111111111111111011111100000000000000110011110100":1,"111111111111111111111011111100011110000111110011110100":3,"111111111111111111111011111100100000001000110111111111":3,"111111111111111111111011111100111110001111110111111111":1,"111111111111111111111111111111000001110000001000000000":1,"111111111111111111111111111111000001110000111011110100":1,"111111111111111111111111111111100001111000111111111111":2,"111111111111111111111111111111111111111111001100001011":2,"111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111":3}],"billed_seconds_reported":0,"observables":[{"label":"kim_theta_0.00pi","x":0,"ideal":1,"measured":-0.03126},{"label":"kim_theta_0.20pi","x":0.2,"ideal":0.45244,"measured":0.00874},{"label":"kim_theta_0.35pi","x":0.35,"ideal":0.11317,"measured":0.04193},{"label":"kim_theta_0.50pi","x":0.5,"ideal":0,"measured":0.00356}],"values":{},"circuit_facts":[{"label":"kim_theta_0.00pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.20pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.35pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.50pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]}],"answer":"The job ran and finished on IQM's free Emerald test device (emerald:mock). The job ID is 01a16484-ece8-7348-add3-d610d2b373a3.\n\nThe test device returns random bits and does not simulate the circuit. Because of that, every measured magnetization came out near zero, whatever the field strength. The measured values were -0.031 at theta = 0, 0.009 at 0.2 pi, 0.042 at 0.35 pi and 0.004 at 0.5 pi. To see the real trend, use the ideal numbers. I computed those with a noise-free simulation of the exact circuits the server received.\n\nWhat I ran:\n- The model was the kicked Ising model on all 54 Emerald qubits. Every qubit started in 0.\n- Each time step put RX(theta) on every qubit. Then it put RZZ(-pi/2) on every coupler that the real Emerald lists today.\n- The real Emerald lists 85 couplers. Its chip has 90, but 5 are not calibrated right now (QB6-QB7, QB15-QB23, QB24-QB32, QB49-QB50 and QB50-QB54). The test device accepts all 85.\n- I ran 3 steps and measured all 54 qubits. There were 4 circuits, one per field strength, with 250 shots each.\n\nI wrote the circuits directly in the chip's native gates, so no compiler step could add, merge or drop a coupler gate. Each RZZ(-pi/2) became exactly one CZ gate. The leftover Z rotations were moved into the phases of the next X rotations. I read the circuits back from the server. Each one has 255 CZ gates, which is 85 couplers times 3 steps, with every coupler used once per step. Each circuit measures QB1 to QB54.\n\nIdeal magnetization, from the noise-free simulation:\n- theta = 0: 1.000. With no sideways field, every spin stays up.\n- theta = 0.2 pi: 0.452.\n- theta = 0.35 pi: 0.113.\n- theta = 0.5 pi: 0.000.\n\nHow I checked the ideal numbers: a qubit's result after 3 steps depends only on qubits at most 2 couplers away, which is up to 13 qubits. So each qubit can be simulated exactly. I checked this method against a full simulation of a 20-qubit piece of the chip. The two agreed to within 1e-13. I also confirmed that my native-gate circuit matches the RX and RZZ version.\n\nWhat it shows: a stronger sideways field tips the spins away from up, and the coupling between neighbors spreads that disorder through the sheet. Magnetization falls from 1 with no field to about 0.45 at 0.2 pi and about 0.11 at 0.35 pi. It reaches exactly 0 at 0.5 pi, where the sheet's magnetization has fully melted. A perfect quantum computer would show this falling curve. The test device shows about 0 everywhere because its answers are random. Running the same job on the real Emerald would show how much of the curve survives the chip's noise. That run would cost credits, so I did not do it.\n\nThe scripts and results are in /Users/claytonchancey/Desktop/quantum/.claude/worktrees/wf_8d7e6233-d69-14/work/ (kim.py, run.py, analyze.py, result.json). The job ID is also in /Users/claytonchancey/Desktop/quantum/.claude/worktrees/wf_8d7e6233-d69-14/job_log.txt."}
